# The Orders API's happy paths. Run the requests top to bottom: later ones use the ids earlier
# ones remember. `make http-env` writes the environment (the API URL and a token per demo user)
# to http-client.private.env.json; pick its `local` (or `aws-dev`) environment. Tokens expire
# after 15 minutes: run `make http-env` again for fresh ones.
# Runs in IntelliJ IDEA / PyCharm (built in) and with httpyac (VS Code extension or CLI).

### Health: public, no token, never rate limited
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/health

### alice (USER) creates an order: 201, with ETag and RateLimit-* headers
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currency": "EUR",
  "items": [
    { "sku": "ABC-123", "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": 1999 },
    { "sku": "XYZ-9", "quantity": 3, "unitPrice": 250 }
  ]
}

> {% client.global.set("orderId", response.body.id); %}

### alice reads her order: 200, ETag "1"
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### alice lists her own orders, newest first, five per page (follow nextCursor for more)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?limit=5
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### The manager (ORDER_MANAGER) lists everyone's orders
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?limit=5
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}

### The manager confirms alice's order, guarded by its version: 200, ETag "2"
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: "1"

{ "status": "CONFIRMED" }

### The manager ships it: 200, ETag "3"
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "SHIPPED" }

### Asking again for the status it already has changes nothing: 200, still ETag "3"
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "SHIPPED" }

### alice creates another order: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "currency": "USD", "items": [ { "sku": "KONE-1", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 5000 } ] }

> {% client.global.set("cancelOrderId", response.body.id); %}

### alice cancels it: an owner may cancel their own order until it ships
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{cancelOrderId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "CANCELLED" }

### The admin (ADMIN) deletes the shipped order: 204, in any status
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### ... after which it is a 404 for everyone
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
